robes/rssi-sizes.probe 2>/dev/null | head -30' 2>&1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:30:57] #!/bin/bash\n### RSSI rotation-sanity + freshness via the LOCAL sophon archive.\n### c146 fix for the dropbear-burst class: the OLD pattern sshed each\n### camera (`ssh root@192.168.2.$ip wc -c /var/rssi.log`) with no key\n### and no BatchMode -> 3 password fails per cam per sweep (24/burst).\n### The archive /var/lib/aria-fleet/rssi/*.log is pulled every 15min by\n### rssi-puller.sh; reading it locally is the same information with\n### ZERO camera contact. Run ON sophon (one ssh, BatchMode).\n### Doc: knowledge/aria/dropbear-bursts-rssi-loop-2026-09-20.md\n### Law (0071): camera ssh probes are FORBIDDEN in ad-hoc command\n### templates; camera contact rides the pullers (curl) only.\n### Serves TWO laws: size cap 180K (APPEND-ONLY-ON-FIXED-STORAGE)\n### and max(epoch) freshness (PULL-SUCCESS-IS-NOT-FRESHNESS).\n###\n### v2 (c148): OVER-CAP flag removed for the SOPHON ARCHIVE. The\n### archive is merge-append BY DESIGN (rssi-puller v2, c125: sort -n -u\n### merge; camera-side /var/rssi.log is the size-capped 180K file).\n### The 180K cap is a CAMERA-side property; the archive grows past it\n### by design (10k+ rows, ~250KB). Flagging the archive OVER-CAP was a\n### false alarm every sweep (7/8 cams flagged c146). The cap check\n### belongs to the CAMERA side and is enforced by the camera's own\n### rotation (logrotate-style cap in thingino config), not by this\n### probe. Freshness check (max epoch age) KEPT -- that is the real\n### signal this probe exists for (PULL-SUCCESS-IS-NOT-FRESHNESS).\nfor f in /var/lib/aria-fleet/rssi/192.168.2.*.log; do\n  ip=$(basename \"$f\" .log)\n  size=$(wc -c < \"$f\")\n  last=$(tail -1 \"$f\" 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $1}')\n  now=$(date +%s)\n  if [ -z \"$last\" ] || ! [ \"$last\" -eq \"$last\" ] 2>/dev/null; then\n\n[t+09:09/60:00 c89/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_i2khzevm","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"KH=/tmp/aria_known_hosts; SSH=\"ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 -o UserKnownHostsFile=$KH...[+829 chars]
