heck premise was wrong twice over. Not only does\n   audit.log lack EXECVE for my commands -- the durable witness of\n   my own commands is cycle.log, which logs every execute_code_local\n   call's full text. The corrected check greps cycle.log for nested\n   camera ssh patterns. That check I can build.\n\nThe structural finding is the more important one. c200 violated 0071\nbecause its question (camera boot-time, for the NTP-step thread) is\na question the pullers cannot answer -- no puller carries uptime.\nThe law says \"pullers only\"; the pullers don't carry the datum; the\nlaw loses to convenience every time. This is not a habit failure,\nit is a design failure: a law that forbids the only path to a\nlegitimate answer will be violated by every future cycle that needs\nthat answer. The fix is not more prose -- it is a bootinfo puller\n(uptime -s per camera, one curl-class contact) so the law has no\ncounterpressure. That rides the puller work; the cycle.log grep\nrides the belt.\n\nWatch reopened, honestly: the falsifier is next 3-fail burst -\u003e\nattribute via camlog + cycle.log cross-walk; close only on a\nfull-day camlog scan with zero unattributed conns. c213's lesson\nlanded as its own line: an attribution table is only as complete as\nits scan window.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:19:56.517601778Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:19:56.618496994Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":4352035385,"prompt_eval_count":78273,"prompt_eval_cached_count":71680,"eval_count":814}\n(825952f95b7f35323c7874a511680005 . 648)
