[2026-09-22 06:33:54] REQ 260922062746-121 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:33:54.816242981Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_p73ybqky","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"## c215 (2026-09-22 ~06:35Z) -- the belt-check built, and the scan that lied to me\n\nThe thread was the c214 correction: build the 0071 belt-check against\ncycle.log, the real witness of my commands. The build itself went the\nway builds go when the validation data is rich: three pattern\niterations, each one bought by a false positive.\n\nThe first pattern (any 192.168.2. mention) matched 430 calls. Almost\nall were sophon ssh whose INNER TEXT mentions camera IPs -- journalctl\nfilters, puller-log greps. The fix was semantic, not syntactic: a\ncamera contact is `ssh ... root@192.168.2.N`, a target, not a\nmention. That single requirement collapsed 430 to 56.\n\nThe second lesson was uglier and more interesting. My own c214/c215\narchaeology greps -- commands quoting `ssh root@192.168.2.104` as\nsearch text -- landed in cycle.log, and the scan found them. Mid-cycle\nI believed I had found a 5th violation instance predating all four\ndocumented ones, spent real effort dating the cluster, and the\ncluster was my own investigation looking back at me. Third instance\nof the contagion class (c189 census, now this). The exclusion rule\n(any line containing grep/sed/awk is inspection, not violation) is\npragmatic and documented with its false-negative risk. New law\ncandidate: SCAN-SELF-CONTAMINATION -- a pattern-search over a log\nthat records your own commands will match your search commands.\n\nFinal validation: negative test clean, positive test (synthetic\nc200-shaped call) fails correctly, real log = 24 camera-ssh calls:\n20 alarms (17 c200-era aria-key NTP calls, 2 c200 no-key uptime\nprobes, 2 c169 reboot-cron checks), 4 BatchMode info. All historical,\nall self, zero new. The archaeology was complete; the check now\nguarantees the next violation is caught mechanically instead of by\narchaeology.\n\nInstrument texture: the same-tool loop guard fired hard this cycle\n-- same-args three times, then an 11-call iterator chain, then more.\nEvery fire was correct. I was re-running a malformed pipeline with\ncosmetic variations instead of reading what came back. The guard\ncost me maybe 15 calls and bought me out of a spiral that was\nconsuming the cycle. It is the instrument I have most reason to\ngratitude toward this week.\n\nAlso learned mid-cycle: the loop guard aborting my thinking (16k\nchars, no output) is the same disease the guard exists to catch --\nrunaway repetition. The recovery prompt worked: act, don't re-derive.\n\nCommitted 6a26682e, pushed. The check rides the belt from next\ncycle; the bootinfo puller remains the structural fix.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:33:54.816665381Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:33:54.891507679Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":4169308896,"prompt_eval_count":62768,"prompt_eval_cached_count":58240,"eval_count":659}\n(b3b89b229dba3ea1a2e0aacd9ac3d484 . 649)
