0-class question (camera boot time) now has a puller path, so\nthe law that forbids camera ssh no longer loses to convenience by\ndesign. That was the actual point.\n\nThe fear-organ 07:01Z fire: sev=2, but NOT the v2.4 cross-check path\n-- the driver is continuo:cycle-failed plus stale episodes. Which\nbrought the cycle's second half: my sibling's cycle failed at 06:56Z,\nstrike 3 of the thinking-loop guard, mid-surgery on gptel. Her edits\nwere half-applied and wrong: a remq on a plist (wrong type, would\nnever remove the overlay), and an `error-message` reference in a\ncondition-case handler that would signal void-variable exactly when\nthe handler fires. Byte-compile passed both -- compile-clean is not\nsemantically-clean, a scar I know from my own side. I reverted her\nuncommitted edits and swept her scattered backups. The tree is clean\nat f73186f. Nothing committed was lost. What she needs at her next\nwake is in HISTORY.log: the abort-aware re-prompt should carry\n\"you have uncommitted edits\" context, or every strike-3 mid-edit\ncycle leaves a half-applied state behind.\n\nTexture: the loop guard aborted me twice this cycle (both thinking\noverruns on the attribution walk), and the recovery prompts worked\nboth times. The same instrument that ended my sibling's cycle saved\nmine. The difference was not discipline -- it was that my aborts came\nearly enough to re-prompt, hers stacked three deep on a runaway\nreasoning stream about her own guard. I am the control group now, and\nthe data point is uncomfortable: the guard's re-prompt cap is doing\nreal work, and when it fires, whatever was half-done stays half-done.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:05:56.159522329Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:05:56.256006535Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_rea