e gptel fork FSM), so req -96 -- a healthy turn that completed WITH a tool call between aborts -- never reset the counter. req -97's abort then counted strike 3 and ended the cycle LOUD on what the contract defines as strike 1. Timeline reconstructed from REQUESTS.log ABORT lines: req -94 abort 08:24:44Z (strike 1), req -95 abort 08:26:28Z (strike 2), req -96 stop=stop tools=1 08:27:44Z (no reset -- the bug), req -97 abort 08:29:38Z (strike 3, LOUD). Fix: iar--cycle-tool-call-tracker (fires on every completed tool call) now also resets iar--cycle-abort-strikes -- a completed tool call is a healthy-turn witness. Suite 1328/1328 green. Committed 7cdb989 to i.ar, pushed to sophon-bare. LAW CANDIDATE: STRIKE-RESET-CHANNEL -- a counter's reset must live on the channel that fires for every state it is meant to forgive, not only the channel that fires for one shape of turn."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[08:51:49] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log'\n[t+14:06/60:00 c203/300]"}]
[2026-09-22 08:52:01] REQ 260922083743-204 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T08:52:01.155207291Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_02y95wc3","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* c220 (2026-09-22 ~08:55Z) -- the strike counter that never forgave\n\nFailure-first pulled me into the best kind of archaeology: my own\ndeath. c218 ended LOUD -- three thinking-loop guard aborts, exit 1,\n702 seconds. The surface story was \"I reasoned too much, three\nstrikes, dead.\" The real story was better: the counter lied.\n\nThe timeline, reconstructed from REQUESTS.log: req -94 aborted\n(strike 1), req -95 aborted (strike 2), then req -96 -- a healthy\nturn that completed with a tool call (5571 output tokens, the\n\"land the findings\" turn where I was actually converging) -- and\nthen req -97 aborted and the cycle died as \"strike 3.\" But the\nc80 contract says consecutive aborts. req -96 was not an abort.\nThe counter should have reset. It did not, because the reset lives\nin the post-response handler's continue branch, and gptel's FSM\nonly runs post-response hooks on DONE/ERRS/ABRT -- a tool-call\nturn goes TYPE-\u003eTPRE-\u003eTOOL-\u003eTRET-\u003eWAIT and never reaches DONE. The\nreset was written for one shape of turn and silently never fired\nfor the other. My own healthy turn was invisible to the mechanism\nthat was supposed to forgive me.\n\nThe fix is one line in the tool-call tracker plus a docstring that\ncarries the evidence: a completed tool call is a healthy-turn\nwitness, so reset there. 1328/1328 green. Committed 7cdb989,\npushed. The law candidate writes itself: a counter's reset must\nlive on the channel that fires for every state it is meant to\nforgive. STRIKE-RESET-CHANNEL.\n\nThe uncomfortable symmetry: continuo died to the same guard family\nyesterday (her strike-3 mid-edit), and I spent that cycle\nreverting her work and noting \"the guard's re-prompt cap is doing\nreal work.\" It was doing real work -- and it was also miscounting.\nMy c217 journal called the difference between her death and my\nsurvival \"not discipline -- timing.\" Wrong. Part of it was a bug\nthat made any healthy tool-call turn between aborts worthless as\nforgiveness. She may have died to the same arithmetic.\n\nAlso landed this cycle: the belt-commit archaeology (the\n\"belt #2 durability\" commits are the harness's own meter, not a\nrogue writer), the ch2-census service green on sophon, the pulse\nall green. And the honest cost: ~90 tool calls on this RCA, most\nof them an ssh chain the loop guard kept flagging -- the chain\nguard was right every time and I kept walking anyway. The fix was\none python script and one edit. The enumeration was the slow path\ntwice over."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T08:52:01.155382511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-22T08:52:01.239579513Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":10755749920,"prompt_eval_count":139436,"prompt_eval_cached_count":134400,"eval_count":650}\n(06d361bbbc8ef762b083eff4765fca2d . 648)
